#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aq-capabilities — AQ-OS Capability Manifest & Shared Toolchain Readiness CLI.

ST-3 & ST-4 (.agents/plans/factory-shared-toolchain/DESIGN.md):
The capability manifest is a RECORD for reproducibility and readiness reporting,
never a runtime gate. A running agent reaches any tool live via `aq-tool <pkg>`
with no restart and no permission check.

This CLI provides:
1. `aq-capabilities list` (default): inspect declared tools and their availability state.
2. `aq-capabilities add <pkg>`: append a required/used tool to the manifest mid-session.
3. `aq-capabilities contribute <pkg>`: open a governed toolchain contribution proposal (ST-4).
4. `aq-capabilities check`: preflight readiness scan (WARN on declared-but-missing).
5. `aq-capabilities overview`: unified view of AQ-OS capabilities (tools, skills, workflows, roles).

Usage:
  aq-capabilities                       List declared tools and availability status
  aq-capabilities list [--json]         List declared tools with availability checks
  aq-capabilities add <pkg> [--name <name>] [--category <cat>] [--required]
                                        Append a tool to the project capability manifest
  aq-capabilities contribute <pkg> [--name <name>] [--profile <prof>] [--justification <msg>]
                                        Open a governed toolchain contribution proposal (ST-4)
  aq-capabilities check [--strict]      Run preflight readiness check (WARNs on missing)
  aq-capabilities overview [--json]     Full AQ-OS capability inventory summary
  aq-capabilities --help                Show this help message
"""

